        "id": 1786377
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-10T05:09:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`page_range_helper.c` uses `rust_shrink_free_page()` exposed from `page_range.rs` and expose `rust_shrink_free_page_wrap()` to `page_range.rs`.\nIf they are both c files then a header make sense, but I don\u0027t know what\u0027s the best practice for rust/c interop.",
      "parentUuid": "e2718214_f73a52b9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 8,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 8,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "12ca4863ade580ca5a5164a3cd491f531efb1a35",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "afb5278d_8b5e45ff",
        "filename": "drivers/android/binder/page_range_helper.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 8,
      "author": {
        "id": 1892347
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-10T05:51:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right now Rust accesses it with an explicit declaration:\n```\nextern \"C\" {\n    fn rust_shrink_free_page_wrap(\n        item: *mut bindings::list_head,\n        list: *mut bindings::list_lru_one,\n        lock: *mut bindings::spinlock_t,\n        cb_arg: *mut kernel::ffi::c_void,\n    ) -\u003e bindings::lru_status;\n}\n```\nWe could probably get rid of this one using the header file, but that requires that the header file is included in `rust/bindings/bindings_helper.h`.",
      "parentUuid": "904b8be7_82e1a461",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 8,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 8,
        "endChar": 34
